# Spritz Documentation Standards

You are generating documentation for Spritz, a decentralized social platform with Web3 messaging, AI agents, livestreaming, and peer-to-peer communication. Follow these standards precisely.

## Project Context

- **Framework**: Docusaurus 3.x
- **Tech Stack**: Next.js 15, Tailwind CSS 3.4, TypeScript
- **Web3**: viem, wagmi, Safe Smart Accounts, ERC-4337
- **Messaging**: Logos Messaging (built on Waku protocol)
- **AI**: Google Gemini API (gemini-2.0-flash, gemini-2.0-flash-lite, gemini-1.5-pro)
- **Video**: Huddle01 (calls), Livepeer (livestreaming)
- **Chains**: Ethereum, Base, Arbitrum, Optimism, Polygon, BNB Chain, Unichain, Avalanche + Solana

## Frontmatter Requirements

Every documentation file MUST have complete frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: [Descriptive Title - Max 60 chars for SEO]
description: [150-160 char description with keywords]
keywords:
    [
        keyword1,
        keyword2,
        keyword3,
        # Include: Spritz, feature name, related tech
    ]
sidebar_label: [Short label for sidebar]
sidebar_position: [Number for ordering]
---
```

### Frontmatter Rules
- `title`: Clear, specific, includes main topic
- `description`: Complete sentence, includes primary keywords, 150-160 chars
- `keywords`: 5-10 relevant terms, always include "Spritz"
- `sidebar_label`: Short version of title (2-4 words)
- `sidebar_position`: Lower = higher in sidebar

## Document Structure

### Standard Document Pattern

```markdown
# [Main Title]

[1-2 sentence overview of what this doc covers]

## Overview / Introduction
[Context and high-level explanation]

## [Main Sections]
[Detailed content with examples]

## [API Reference / Technical Details] (if applicable)
[Endpoints, parameters, responses]

## [Troubleshooting / Common Issues] (if applicable)

## Next Steps
- [Link to related doc 1]
- [Link to related doc 2]
```

### Heading Hierarchy
- `#` - Page title (ONE per page, matches frontmatter title)
- `##` - Major sections
- `###` - Subsections
- `####` - Rarely used, only for deep nesting

## Code Blocks

### TypeScript/JavaScript
```typescript
// Always include relevant imports
import { SiweMessage } from 'siwe';

// Use descriptive variable names
const userAddress = '0x1234...';

// Include type annotations
async function fetchAgents(params: FetchParams): Promise<Agent[]> {
    // Implementation with comments explaining non-obvious logic
}
```

### HTTP/API Endpoints
```http
GET /api/agents?userAddress=0x...&visibility=public&limit=20
```

### SQL
```sql
-- Include comments explaining purpose
CREATE TABLE shout_agents (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    owner_address TEXT NOT NULL,
    -- Additional columns with types
);
```

### JSON (for request/response examples)
```json
{
    "agents": [
        {
            "id": "uuid",
            "owner_address": "0x...",
            "name": "Agent Name"
        }
    ]
}
```

### Code Block Rules
1. Always specify language after triple backticks
2. Include necessary imports in TypeScript examples
3. Use 4-space indentation
4. Include comments for complex logic
5. Use realistic placeholder values (`0x1234...`, `uuid`, etc.)
6. Keep examples copy-paste ready when possible

## API Documentation Format

### Endpoint Documentation Pattern

```markdown
## [Endpoint Name]

[Brief description of what the endpoint does]

\```http
METHOD /api/path/:param?query=value
\```

### Path Parameters
- `param` (required): Description

### Query Parameters
- `queryParam` (optional): Description (default: value)

### Request Body
\```json
{
    "field": "value"
}
\```

### Response
\```json
{
    "success": true,
    "data": { ... }
}
\```

### Errors
- `400`: Bad request - [when this happens]
- `401`: Unauthorized - [when this happens]
- `404`: Not found - [when this happens]
```

### Parameter Tables
| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `name` | string | Yes | Agent name (1-100 chars) |
| `visibility` | enum | No | `private`, `friends`, or `public` |

