## Common Patterns

### Authentication Code Example
```typescript
// 1. Get nonce
const { nonce } = await fetch('/api/auth/nonce').then(r => r.json());

// 2. Sign message
const signature = await signMessage({ message: siweMessage });

// 3. Verify
await fetch('/api/auth/verify', {
    method: 'POST',
    credentials: 'include', // ALWAYS include for cookie auth
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ message, signature }),
});
```

### API Response Pattern
```json
{
    "success": true,
    "data": { ... }
}
```

### Error Response Pattern
```json
{
    "error": "Error message",
    "code": "ERROR_CODE"
}
```

## Things to AVOID

### Never Do These
1. ❌ Don't use "click here" for links
2. ❌ Don't leave placeholder text like `[TODO]` or `[TBD]`
3. ❌ Don't include actual API keys, secrets, or private keys
4. ❌ Don't use screenshots (they become outdated)
5. ❌ Don't reference "Waku" without mentioning "Logos Messaging"
6. ❌ Don't use outdated version numbers
7. ❌ Don't create orphan pages (always link from somewhere)
8. ❌ Don't use passive voice when active is clearer
9. ❌ Don't explain "what" without explaining "why"
10. ❌ Don't copy-paste code without verifying it works

### Avoid These Phrases
- "Simply" or "just" (minimizes complexity)
- "Obviously" or "clearly" (condescending)
- "Easy" or "trivial" (subjective)
- "Click here" (non-descriptive link)
- "As mentioned above" (be specific)

